-# fastunknot 0.3.0: structural certificates and optional shared backends
+# fastunknot 0.4.0: continuation quotients and certified algebraic splitting
+
+Version 0.4.0 adds two opt-in scanner backends and an exact bounded-window
+crossing-order optimizer. The standard backend remains the default.
+
+```sh
+python -m fastunknot recognize examples/conway.json --backend barcode
+python -m fastunknot recognize examples/conway.json --backend fitting
+python -m fastunknot khovanov examples/conway.json --barcode
+python -m fastunknot khovanov examples/conway.json --fitting
+python -m fastunknot recognize examples/conway.json --backend fitting --order-window 10 --order-passes 2
+python -m unittest discover -s tests -v
+```
+
+The recognition backend `barcode` exactly decomposes whole common-nilpotent
+components into interval complexes, then shortens intervals to at most two
+objects using the proved continuation theorem. `fitting` first looks for
+hidden direct summands by solving scalar chain-endomorphism equations; every
+accepted basis change is independently verified inside the implementation.
+Both recognition backends retain only final unreduced rank capped at three.
+
+The `khovanov --barcode` and `khovanov --fitting` routes retain full interval
+lengths and return exact total ranks and raw homological-degree counts. They
+exclude decision caps. Neither new backend retains quantum grading. New exact
+backend flags are mutually exclusive with `--shared` and with each other;
+unsupported pivot/algebra, tail, or factor combinations are rejected.
+
+The optional order optimizer minimizes the peak frontier and then frontier
+mass in each chosen window. Window optimization is disabled by default;
+`--order-window 10 --order-passes 2` enables it and charges its time to the
+recognition budget. A smaller ordering objective does not guarantee a shorter
+full computation.
+
+All 94 unit tests passed in the recorded environment. The companion package
+also contains a recognizer-independent dense verifier (861 dual-number
+complexes, 10,206 threshold comparisons), actual-diagram split certificates,
+and 285 interleaved benchmark calls. Certified splitting reduces algebraic
+work on several cases, but has no demonstrated general wall-clock advantage.
+No nontrivial actual-diagram component in that corpus qualified for interval
+shortening; synthetic examples and the proof establish that feature's current
+scope. The new backends therefore remain research options.
+
+The article proves a conditional bound in frontier size and the distance
+between certified interval checkpoints. **A general quasi-polynomial unknot
+recognition algorithm is not established.** A resource limit returns `UNKNOWN`.
+
+Public recognition accepts
+`--backend standard|shared|saturated|euler|barcode|fitting`.
+The main new modules are `barcode_scan.py`, `scalar_split.py`, and `order_dp.py`.
+The package-level README and REPRODUCING document describe the two integration
+patches, source references, mathematical guarantees, and reproduction steps.
+
+## Version 0.3 history
+
+The following section describes inherited structural compression. Its test
+counts and measurements refer to that preceding version.
+
+### fastunknot 0.3.0: structural certificates and optional shared backends
 
 This research continuation adds a linear signed Seifert-graph certificate before
 the established recognition pipeline and three optional Khovanov backends.
